This is a partial theory of thinking.... Whenever one encounters a new situation (or makes a substantial change in one’s viewpoint), he selects from memory a structure called a frame; a remembered framework to be adapted to fit reality by changing details as necessary. A frame ... [represents] a stereotyped situation, like being in a certain kind of living room, or going to a child’s birthday party.
